tutorial-items-name = Items and Survival

## Entities

ent-TutorialHoloMentorItems = N.A.N.C.I.
    .desc = A holographic training intelligence. She is projected from the nearest holopad, and is very pleased you asked.
ent-TutorialCommemorativePlaque = commemorative plaque
    .desc = Dedicated to the applicants of Wing Five, whose contributions to Nanotrasen safety procedure were both insignificant and involuntary.
ent-TutorialGearLocker = supply locker
    .desc = A locker. It is not locked. Nanotrasen ran out of locks before it ran out of lockers.
ent-TutorialTrainingDrink = training can
    .desc = Designated for training use only, do not drink.
ent-TutorialPullCrate = supply crate
    .desc = Too big for any bag you will ever be issued. Drag it.
ent-TutorialBreachCue = tutorial breach cue
    .desc = Sets off a charge against the hull when the breach beat begins.

## Goal titles

tutorial-items-goal-dexterity = Manual Dexterity
tutorial-items-goal-objects = Object Familiarisation
tutorial-items-goal-context = Contextual Interaction
tutorial-items-goal-storage = Storage and Stowage
tutorial-items-goal-belt = Equipment Allocation
tutorial-items-goal-provisions = Vacuum Certification
tutorial-items-goal-certification = Certification

## Chamber 1. hands, tools and the girder

tutorial-items-sg-welcome = Listen to N.A.N.C.I.
tutorial-items-nanci-welcome-1 = Welcome back to the Nanotrasen Employee Onboarding Facility.
tutorial-items-nanci-welcome-2 = You have been assigned to Wing Five: Applied Manipulation.
tutorial-items-nanci-welcome-3 = Wing Five teaches you to touch things.
tutorial-items-nanci-welcome-4 = Wing Six teaches you which things not to touch, but it is closed for repairs.

tutorial-items-sg-take-tool = Pick up a tool.
tutorial-items-control-take-tool = Click an item to pick it up.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-tool-1 = There is a girder in the middle of this chamber. It is in the way of the exit.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-tool-2 = Take it apart. The table has a wrench and a screwdriver.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-tool-3 = Those are the tools you need for the job.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-tool-4 = Pick them up.

tutorial-items-sg-swap-hands = Switch to your other hand.
tutorial-items-control-swap-hands = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="SwapHands"][/bold][/color] to switch your active hand.
tutorial-items-nanci-swap-hands-1 = Most people have two hands. Switch to the other one.
tutorial-items-nanci-swap-hands-2 = Hands are one of the few things Nanotrasen issues in pairs.

tutorial-items-sg-take-other-tool = Pick up the other tool.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-other-tool-1 = Now pick up the other tool.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-other-tool-2 = You should have a tool in each hand now.

tutorial-items-sg-brief-girder = Listen to N.A.N.C.I.
tutorial-items-nanci-brief-girder-1 = The girder comes apart in two stages.
tutorial-items-nanci-brief-girder-2 = Wrench first, screwdriver second.
tutorial-items-nanci-brief-girder-3 = Whichever tool is in your active hand is the tool you are using. Nothing else is consulted.

tutorial-items-sg-wrench-active = Hold the wrench in your active hand.
tutorial-items-control-wrench-active = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="SwapHands"][/bold][/color] to switch your active hand.
tutorial-items-nanci-wrench-active-1 = You now need to switch to the wrench.

tutorial-items-sg-unbolt-girder = Unanchor the girder with the wrench.
tutorial-items-control-unbolt-girder = Click an item while holding a tool to use the tool on it.
tutorial-items-nanci-unbolt-girder-1 = Unbolt it with the wrench.

tutorial-items-sg-driver-active = Hold the screwdriver in your active hand.
tutorial-items-control-driver-active = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="SwapHands"][/bold][/color] to switch your active hand.
tutorial-items-nanci-driver-active-1 = Now switch to the screwdriver.

tutorial-items-sg-strip-girder = Take the girder apart with the screwdriver.
tutorial-items-nanci-strip-girder-1 = Take it apart.
tutorial-items-nanci-strip-girder-2 = Engineering usually does not like it when you take apart walls.
tutorial-items-nanci-strip-girder-3 = This is an exception.

tutorial-items-sg-drop-tools = Drop both tools.
tutorial-items-control-drop-tools = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="Drop"][/bold][/color] to drop the item in your active hand.
tutorial-items-nanci-drop-tools-1 = The girder is gone. The chamber is now less obstructed than it was.
tutorial-items-nanci-drop-tools-2 = Put both tools down.
tutorial-items-nanci-drop-tools-3 = One hand at a time.
tutorial-items-nanci-drop-tools-4 = I understand your emotional attachment to these tools, but you will not need them going forward.

## Chamber 2. examining and using

tutorial-items-sg-examine-plaque = Examine the plaque.
tutorial-items-control-examine-plaque = Use [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="ExamineEntity"][/bold][/color] to examine something.
tutorial-items-nanci-examine-plaque-1 = This chamber contains a commemorative plaque.
tutorial-items-nanci-examine-plaque-2 = Examine it.
tutorial-items-nanci-examine-plaque-3 = Examining is how you learn what a thing is before it learns what you are.
tutorial-items-nanci-examine-plaque-4 = It costs nothing and has saved more lives than the medical department.

tutorial-items-sg-take-lantern = Pick up the lantern.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-lantern-1 = Thank you for reading. Nobody reads.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-lantern-2 = There is a lantern on the table.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-lantern-3 = Pick it up.

tutorial-items-sg-light-lantern = Turn the lantern on.
tutorial-items-control-light-lantern = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="ActivateItemInHand"][/bold][/color] to use the item in your active hand.
tutorial-items-nanci-light-lantern-1 = Oops.
tutorial-items-nanci-light-lantern-2 = The lighting in this chamber has failed.
tutorial-items-nanci-light-lantern-3 = Be sure to complain at the engineering department on your way out.
tutorial-items-nanci-light-lantern-4 = Many items do something when you use them in your hand.
tutorial-items-nanci-light-lantern-5 = That lantern is one of them. Turn it on.

## Chamber 3. locker, can and bin

tutorial-items-sg-open-locker = Open the locker.
tutorial-items-control-open-locker = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="ActivateItemInWorld"][/bold][/color] on something to use it.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-locker-1 = Some things are too large to pick up.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-locker-2 = Lockers, consoles, vending machines, most of Cargo.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-locker-3 = You use those where they stand.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-locker-4 = Open the locker.

tutorial-items-sg-take-can = Pick up the can.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-can-1 = There is a can inside.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-can-2 = Pick up that can.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-can-3 = If nothing is happening, your active hand is still holding a lantern. You know the remedy.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-can-4 = I said, pick up that can.

tutorial-items-sg-throw-can = Throw the can at the disposal unit.
tutorial-items-control-throw-can = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="ThrowItemInHand"][/bold][/color] while hovering you want it to go.
tutorial-items-nanci-throw-can-1 = Now put it in the trash can.
tutorial-items-nanci-throw-can-2 = There is a disposal unit across the chamber.
tutorial-items-nanci-throw-can-3 = You may throw it. Nanotrasen encourages efficiency.
tutorial-items-nanci-throw-can-4 = It has to land inside. Efficiency is not the same as permission to miss.

tutorial-items-sg-bin-can = Get the can into the disposal unit.
tutorial-items-nanci-bin-can-1 = If you miss, pick it up and throw it again.
tutorial-items-nanci-bin-can-2 = Keep going until it lands inside.
tutorial-items-nanci-bin-can-3 = You may also walk over and put it in by hand, but you will lose your dignity.

tutorial-items-sg-flush-bin = Flush the disposal unit.
tutorial-items-control-flush-bin = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="AltActivateItemInWorld"][/bold][/color] on something for its alternate action.
tutorial-items-nanci-flush-bin-1 = Now flush it.
tutorial-items-nanci-flush-bin-2 = Most objects have a second action that ordinary activation will never reach.
tutorial-items-nanci-flush-bin-3 = Flushing is one. So is climbing, like you learned in our previous training.
tutorial-items-nanci-flush-bin-4 = The alternate action is worth trying on everything, exactly once.

## Chamber 4. bag, plushie and pulling

tutorial-items-sg-take-plushie = Pick up the lizard plushie.
tutorial-items-control-take-plushie = Click an item to pick it up.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-plushie-1 = Nanotrasen wellness policy requires every employee to be issued one companion asset.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-plushie-2 = That is the companion asset. Pick it up.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-plushie-3 = It says weh. That is its function.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-plushie-4 = It performs that function reliably, which puts it ahead of most of your colleagues.

tutorial-items-sg-open-bag = Open your bag.
tutorial-items-control-open-bag = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="OpenBackpack"][/bold][/color] to open the bag on your back.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-bag-1 = You are wearing a bag.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-bag-2 = You have been wearing it this entire time.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-bag-3 = Open it.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-bag-4 = This is where having only two hands stops being your problem.

tutorial-items-sg-stow-plushie = Put the plushie in your bag.
tutorial-items-control-stow-plushie = Hold an item and press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="SmartEquipBackpack"][/bold][/color] to stow it, or open the bag and click it in.
tutorial-items-nanci-stow-plushie-1 = Put the companion asset in the bag.
tutorial-items-nanci-stow-plushie-2 = A bag holds a great deal more than your hands do.

tutorial-items-sg-retrieve-plushie = Take the plushie back out.
tutorial-items-nanci-retrieve-plushie-1 = Now take it back out.
tutorial-items-nanci-retrieve-plushie-2 = This is how you quickly move items in and out of your bag.

tutorial-items-sg-keep-plushie = Put the plushie away for good.
tutorial-items-nanci-keep-plushie-1 = Put it away and leave it there. It is yours now.
tutorial-items-nanci-keep-plushie-2 = Companion assets are not deducted from your pay.
tutorial-items-nanci-keep-plushie-3 = You may keep it until the end of your shift.

tutorial-items-sg-pull-crate = Pull the crate.
tutorial-items-control-pull-crate = Press [color=#FFD25A][bold][keybind="TryPullObject"][/bold][/color] on something to pull it.
tutorial-items-nanci-pull-crate-1 = Some things do not go in a bag.
tutorial-items-nanci-pull-crate-2 = Crates. Lockers. Colleagues.
tutorial-items-nanci-pull-crate-3 = You drag those.
tutorial-items-nanci-pull-crate-4 = Grab a hold of the crate.

tutorial-items-sg-park-crate = Park the crate on the marked square and let go.
tutorial-items-control-park-crate = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="ReleasePulledObject"][/bold][/color] to let go of what you are dragging.
tutorial-items-nanci-park-crate-1 = Drag it to the marked square.
tutorial-items-nanci-park-crate-2 = You will move slower when you are dragging.
tutorial-items-nanci-park-crate-3 = Let go of it in the marked area.

## Chamber 5. tool belt

tutorial-items-sg-take-belt = Pick up the tool belt.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-belt-1 = This chamber contains a tool belt, and a crowbar you will want shortly.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-belt-2 = Take the belt.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-belt-3 = If this fails your active hand already has something in it.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-belt-4 = We already went over this. You know the remedy.

tutorial-items-sg-wear-belt = Put the tool belt in your belt slot.
tutorial-items-control-wear-belt = Click the belt into the belt slot in your inventory.
tutorial-items-nanci-wear-belt-1 = Put it on.
tutorial-items-nanci-wear-belt-2 = Not by using it. Using a belt opens the belt, which is a different and less useful outcome.
tutorial-items-nanci-wear-belt-3 = It goes in the slot on your person that is shaped like a belt.
tutorial-items-nanci-wear-belt-4 = The belt is not fashionable. Nothing you will ever be issued is fashionable.

tutorial-items-sg-belt-crowbar = Put the crowbar on your belt.
tutorial-items-control-belt-crowbar = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="SmartEquipBelt"][/bold][/color] to stow it on your belt.
tutorial-items-nanci-belt-crowbar-1 = There is a crowbar on the table.
tutorial-items-nanci-belt-crowbar-2 = Put it on the belt.
tutorial-items-nanci-belt-crowbar-3 = You already know what a crowbar is for.
tutorial-items-nanci-belt-crowbar-4 = You might need it sooner than you expect.

tutorial-items-sg-open-belt = Open the tool belt.
tutorial-items-control-open-belt = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="OpenBelt"][/bold][/color] to open the belt you are wearing.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-belt-1 = The crowbar is on the belt now.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-belt-2 = Open the belt.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-belt-3 = A belt is a bit like a bag, except only specific items fit in it.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-belt-4 = That is the whole difference between a belt and a bag.

## Chamber 6. the suit, the survival box, the breach and the crossing

tutorial-items-sg-wear-suit = Put the pressure suit on.
tutorial-items-control-wear-suit = Click the suit into the outer clothing slot in your inventory.
tutorial-items-stuck-wear-suit = Pick the suit up from the emergency closet, then click it into the outer clothing slot. Using it in your hand does not put it on.
tutorial-items-nanci-wear-suit-1 = There is an emergency closet. It holds a pressure suit.
tutorial-items-nanci-wear-suit-2 = Open it and put the suit on.
tutorial-items-nanci-wear-suit-3 = Not by using it. Using a suit in your hand does not put a suit on.
tutorial-items-nanci-wear-suit-4 = It goes in the slot on your person that is shaped like a coat.
tutorial-items-nanci-wear-suit-5 = It is rated for vacuum, and the disappointment of your supervisor.

tutorial-items-sg-deploy-helmet = Deploy the suit helmet.
tutorial-items-control-deploy-helmet = Click the hotbar action, or right-click the worn suit and choose deploy.
tutorial-items-stuck-deploy-helmet = The helmet folds into the suit collar when clicked. Deploy it again from the hotbar, or by right-clicking the worn suit.
tutorial-items-nanci-deploy-helmet-1 = The helmet is part of the suit.
tutorial-items-nanci-deploy-helmet-2 = It is folded into the collar, which is another ability you now have.
tutorial-items-nanci-deploy-helmet-3 = Deploy the helmet.
tutorial-items-nanci-deploy-helmet-4 = If you clicked the helmet and it vanished, it folded into the collar.
tutorial-items-nanci-deploy-helmet-5 = Applicant seventeen died because they could not find the helmet.

tutorial-items-sg-find-box = Take the survival box out of your bag.
tutorial-items-control-find-box = Take out your survival box from your bag.
tutorial-items-nanci-find-box-1 = There has been a survival box in your bag this entire time.
tutorial-items-nanci-find-box-2 = You probably did not notice. Nobody notices.
tutorial-items-nanci-find-box-3 = It is the difference between a bad shift and a short one.
tutorial-items-nanci-find-box-4 = Take it out of the bag.

tutorial-items-sg-open-box = Open the survival box.
tutorial-items-control-open-box = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="ActivateItemInHand"][/bold][/color] to open a container you are holding.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-box-1 = Open the box.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-box-2 = It contains a breath mask, a gas tank, and one medipen.
tutorial-items-nanci-open-box-3 = The medipen is not part of today's assessment. Try not to need it.

tutorial-items-sg-empty-hand-for-mask = Switch to your empty hand.
tutorial-items-control-empty-hand-for-mask = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="SwapHands"][/bold][/color] to switch to your empty hand.
tutorial-items-nanci-empty-hand-for-mask-1 = The box is in one hand. Your other hand is the one that can take things out of it.
tutorial-items-nanci-empty-hand-for-mask-2 = Switch to the empty one.

tutorial-items-sg-take-mask = Take the breath mask out of the box.
tutorial-items-control-take-mask = Click the breath mask in the open box.
tutorial-items-stuck-take-mask = This step completes when you are holding the breath mask. Switch to an empty hand, then click the mask in the open box.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-mask-1 = Now take the mask.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-mask-2 = You have done this before.

tutorial-items-sg-wear-mask = Put the breath mask on.
tutorial-items-control-wear-mask = Press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="ActivateItemInHand"][/bold][/color] to put on what you are holding.
tutorial-items-nanci-wear-mask-1 = Now put on the mask.
tutorial-items-nanci-wear-mask-2 = The mask does nothing by itself.
tutorial-items-nanci-wear-mask-3 = This surprises people, usually once.

tutorial-items-sg-take-tank = Take the gas tank out of the box.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-tank-1 = Now the tank.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-tank-2 = The tank does nothing by itself either.
tutorial-items-nanci-take-tank-3 = Together they are the second most important thing you own.

tutorial-items-sg-suit-stow-tank = Put the tank in your back.
tutorial-items-control-suit-stow-tank = Hold the tank in your active hand and press [color=#FFD24A][bold][keybind="SmartEquipSuitStorage"][/bold][/color] to put it in your back.
tutorial-items-nanci-suit-stow-tank-1 = Put the tank into the suit's storage slot.
tutorial-items-nanci-suit-stow-tank-2 = This frees your hand.
tutorial-items-nanci-suit-stow-tank-3 = Free hands are the difference between an incident and an anecdote.

tutorial-items-sg-internals-on = Turn your internals on.
tutorial-items-control-internals-on = Click the Toggle Internals action on your hotbar, or press the associated key to turn it on.
tutorial-items-nanci-internals-on-1 = Carrying that tank has given you an action.
tutorial-items-nanci-internals-on-2 = Some items do that.
tutorial-items-nanci-internals-on-3 = Use it.
tutorial-items-nanci-internals-on-4 = You are now breathing from the tank instead of the room.
tutorial-items-nanci-internals-on-5 = Breathable air in the room is now optional.

tutorial-items-sg-breach-brief = Listen to N.A.N.C.I.
tutorial-items-nanci-breach-brief-1 = The section beyond the airlock is pressurised and comfortable.
tutorial-items-nanci-breach-brief-2 = That is a problem, because I am required to train you.
tutorial-items-nanci-breach-brief-3 = Decompressing chamber in 3.
tutorial-items-nanci-breach-brief-4 = 2.
tutorial-items-nanci-breach-brief-5 = 1.
tutorial-items-nanci-breach-brief-6 = There. The fresh vacuum of space.

tutorial-items-sg-pry-firelock = Pry the firelock open.
tutorial-items-control-pry-firelock = Click the firelock while holding a crowbar.
tutorial-items-nanci-pry-firelock-1 = The firelock has now closed, which is the one part of this facility that works.
tutorial-items-nanci-pry-firelock-2 = It will not open itself with vacuum on the other side.
tutorial-items-nanci-pry-firelock-3 = You have a crowbar. You have had one since chamber 5.
tutorial-items-nanci-pry-firelock-4 = Open it using the crowbar.

tutorial-items-sg-cross-vacuum = Cross the vacuum to the far side.
tutorial-items-nanci-cross-vacuum-1 = Walk through the spaced area.
tutorial-items-nanci-cross-vacuum-2 = Do not stop to admire it.
tutorial-items-nanci-cross-vacuum-3 = You will run out of air.

tutorial-items-sg-internals-off = Turn your internals off.
tutorial-items-control-internals-off = Click the Toggle Internals action on your hotbar, or press the associated key to turn it off.
tutorial-items-nanci-internals-off-1 = You made it through, and this side has air in it.
tutorial-items-nanci-internals-off-2 = Turn the tank off.
tutorial-items-nanci-internals-off-3 = That tank holds minutes, not hours of air.
tutorial-items-nanci-internals-off-4 = It does not refill itself when you stop paying attention.
tutorial-items-nanci-internals-off-5 = People have died by breathing from an empty tank in a room that was full of air.

## Chamber 7. graduation

tutorial-items-sg-graduation = Listen to N.A.N.C.I.
tutorial-items-nanci-graduation-1 = That concludes Applied Manipulation.
tutorial-items-nanci-graduation-2 = You can now pick up, swap, drop, throw, examine, use, stow, wear, pull, and breathe.
tutorial-items-nanci-graduation-3 = You are now theoretically capable of every simple task aboard our stations.
tutorial-items-nanci-graduation-4 = Theoretically.

tutorial-items-sg-farewell = Finish the tutorial.
tutorial-items-nanci-farewell-1 = Please take a moment to enjoy our arcade.
tutorial-items-nanci-farewell-2 = But only a brief moment before you will be called on your next assignment.
tutorial-items-nanci-farewell-3 = I will be watching you from every holopad on the station.

## Unscripted remarks

tutorial-items-nanci-quip-drank = You drank it... That can has been in this chamber since the facility opened. Please check up in Medical after training has concluded.
tutorial-items-nanci-quip-binned = Get out of the unit. You are not a disposable. Applicant eleven is still in a bin somewhere in Cargo.
